output_dir  = "output"
description = [=[mod id 3790290682

[b]Puts the numbers a commander actually needs into the commander tooltips.[/b] Research times, ability cooldowns, structure health and armour, and movement speed, on the tooltip you are already looking at — no alt-tabbing to a wiki mid-round.

[h1]What it adds to tooltips[/h1]

[list]
[*] [b]Research time[/b] — an hourglass and a number on every research and upgrade. Armour 3 reads "40 res, 120 seconds" instead of just "40 res".
[*] [b]Cooldown[/b] — a stopwatch on commander abilities: Bone Wall, Power Surge, Nutrient Mist, Rupture, Heal Wave, Cyst, and the rest.
[*] [b]Health and armour[/b] — for anything you drop, build or manufacture, on both teams.
[*] [b]Movement speed[/b] — for the things that move: ARC, MAC, Drifter, Whip, Shade, Shift, Crag.
[/list]

All of it sits in one row under the tooltip title, above the description. The card grows to fit, and tooltips with nothing extra to show look exactly as they always did.

Health and armour take the game's own selection-panel colours, so a number means the same thing in the tooltip as it does when you click a structure that already exists. Vanilla's selection panel is brought in line too, where it coloured the two figures differently but drew both icons in one flat team colour.

[b]ARC stances.[/b] The Deploy and Undeploy buttons describe the state they put the ARC into, so Deploy shows armour dropping to 0 and speed to 0 — the cost of deploying, visible while you are choosing it.

[h1]The "In Cooldown" panel[/h1]

Commander ability cooldowns in NS2 are [b]team-global[/b]: they are not per-structure and not per-commander. A Shade Ink puts every Shade on cooldown, so three Shades cannot alternate Ink to keep ARCs suppressed.

This mod adds a panel on the right of the screen listing whatever your team has on cooldown right now, using the game's own rotating dial plus the seconds remaining. It is visible to [b]every player on the team[/b], not just the commander. Shade Ink being down is as useful to a field alien deciding whether to push as it is to the commander.

[b]It also fixes a vanilla bug.[/b] In the base game, nobody but the commander who personally cast an ability ever saw its cooldown dial — not a commander who took the chair mid-cooldown, not one who had just left it, and no field player at all. Enforcement was always correct; only the display was blind. Vanilla marks the gap itself, with an empty "send message to commander to sync the cd" block sitting where the sync belongs. The dial on the commander button is now right whoever is in the chair.

[h1]The alien hive panel[/h1]

The hive status panel in the top-left corner (Advanced Options, UI, hive status) already shows each hive's health, eggs and type. Two things are added to every hive's row:

[list]
[*] [b]Biomass[/b] — one icon per +1 biomass research that hive has completed. A fresh hive shows none, the same way it shows no hive type icon until it is upgraded, and each research adds its own button's art.
[*] [b]Researching[/b] — the game's own rotating "working" ring with the DNA glyph inside it, on any hive researching anything: biomass, a lifeform ability, or a hive type upgrade. The same pair you see in the world when you look at a busy hive.
[/list]

Both are visible to every player on the team, not just the commander.

[h1]Fixes to vanilla display bugs[/h1]

[list]
[*] [b]Simultaneous biomass research.[/b] With two hives researching biomass at once the tech map lit up only one icon between them, because the team collapses every hive into a single number before drawing. Two hives now light two icons, three light three.
[*] [b]Supply icons.[/b] The supply figure on a tooltip was marked with a MAC or a Drifter while the HUD's top bar used a different pair of icons for the same thing. The tooltip now uses the top bar's. The MAC and Drifter icons are untouched wherever they stand for the units themselves.
[*] [b]Uncoloured biomass icons.[/b] The biomass icon was drawn as bare greyscale art wherever it appeared: on the commander tooltip, on the spectator counter, and so on the hive panel too. Nothing else in a tooltip or in the tech tree stays uncoloured, so it read as unfinished rather than deliberate. All of them now take the tech map's own colour for researched alien tech.
[*] [b]Lost arms lab upgrades.[/b] When a team loses every arms lab, or they all lose power, the weapon and armour icons on the marine HUD simply vanished - which looks exactly like never having researched them. They now stay on screen in the alert red the base game already defined for this and never showed, so "we lost it" reads differently from "we never had it".
[/list]

[h1]Live values[/h1]

Numbers that change during a round are read live rather than printed from a table. Bone Wall's health scales with your biomass level, so at Biomass 9 the tooltip says 900, not 100.

Movement speed is read off the unit's own class rather than from a table, so it is the vanilla unupgraded figure. Mods that compute speed live from game state rather than storing it will read low, or blank rather than guess.

[h1]The biomass bar[/h1]

The twelve bead bar in the top left, the one that appears with the map, the buy menu or the tech map open, only ever knew whole beads: a bead was empty until the research finished, then full.

Each bead being researched now fills as the work goes in, and more than one fills at a time when more than one hive is working. The ability icons along the bar light up and carry a progress bar while their research is under way, the same as they do on the tech map, instead of staying greyed out until the moment they finish.

[h1]Settings[/h1]

Options, Mods, "Bleu's Improved Tooltips". The In Cooldown panel can be turned off there, and a slider sets the shortest cooldown it will list, so you can quiet it down or show everything. Both take effect immediately.

[h1]Works with other mods[/h1]

Nothing is hardcoded per tech. The mod reads the same tech data the game itself uses to make a tech function, so tech added by other mods gets improved tooltips automatically, with no patch needed here.

[b]Community Balance Mod[/b] is the one mod named anywhere in the code, in a single place: its biomass 5 research is tinted on the hive panel in CBM's own colour for advanced alien tech, matching the way CBM marks that hive out. Everything else about CBM tech, including its own icons for it, arrives through the same path as anything else.

Modders can register their own value resolvers for anything they compute at runtime — see the README on GitHub.

[h1]Servers[/h1]

The mod does not change gameplay. It reads values your client already has. The two things it does send are the team cooldown list the panel is built from, and each hive's biomass and research for the hive panel, neither of which a client can work out for itself.

It does have to be installed on the server. NS2's default consistency check restricts which mod entry files a client is allowed to load, so on a server running stock settings the server needs this mod too. If you want it on a server you play on, ask the admin to add it.

Source: https://github.com/Bleuitup/Bleus-Improved-Tooltips]=]
